<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-haupaix-avian-plumage-somite-stripes-code-traceability> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Haupaix et al. (2018), Inaba et al. (2019) & Lin et al. (2013) somite-prepatterned Agouti signaling, melanocyte gap-junction reaction-diffusion and feather-follicle ring-niche chevrons in galliform plumage stripes — Code-to-model traceability: 86/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-20"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "The module docstring (L1-L83) maps each mechanism to the paper and figure it comes from, states what was corrected and what remains a reduction, and names all five Lean theorems; the section 3b banner (L517-L532) states the modelling assumptions of the follicle reduction; the math KG YAML registers Laws 4-5 with Lean loci and code loci. Deductions: Panel B/C/D and the Pass 2 measurement strings still cite 'Haupaix Figs. 1-2' for mm widths the paper does not report (-6); the 'bead' naming persists in function and variable names (-3); the Lean laws are linked by name but the Python does not assert the integer instances of Theorem 4 (-2); some KG code loci span whole sections rather than the exact lines (-3)." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-code-traceability> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> ;
    pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/code-traceability" ;
    pk:evidenceAgainst "2018-haupaix-avian-plumage-somite-stripes.py L1225–L1242: Measurement strings still attribute the 0.42 mm quail width to 'Haupaix Figs. 1-2' <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/469bf3c/2018-haupaix-avian-plumage-somite-stripes.py#L1225-L1242>" ;
    pk:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-haupaix-avian-plumage-somite-stripes-code-traceability-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-haupaix-avian-plumage-somite-stripes-code-traceability-2>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-haupaix-avian-plumage-somite-stripes-code-traceability-3> ;
    pk:hasScore 8.6e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-haupaix-avian-plumage-somite-stripes-model-fidelity> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Haupaix et al. (2018), Inaba et al. (2019) & Lin et al. (2013) somite-prepatterned Agouti signaling, melanocyte gap-junction reaction-diffusion and feather-follicle ring-niche chevrons in galliform plumage stripes — Model fidelity to source: 78/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-20"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "The two-step Haupaix mechanism is now implemented end-to-end: somite prepattern -> dermal agouti band -> dose-dependent yellow-pulse duration -> feather type (b / y / fully pheomelanic), with the Lin (2013) ring niche and opened-cylinder chevron geometry (`niche_feather_type`, `niche_yellow_pulse_duty`, `build_feather_follicle_lattice`, `simulate_follicle_niche_cylinder`, L545-L724) and five Lean theorems (0 sorrys). Deductions: the PDE integrates a cubic-saturating linearisation around (0.46, 0.46) while the docstring/JSON write rational Gierer-Meinhardt kinetics (-6); the species widths come from an analytic Gaussian-threshold formula with an unexplained 1.13 sigma factor, not from the PDE, whose own yellow fraction is 0.35, not 0.44 (-5); the 'bead' dose-response is a fitted exponential (-3); the follicle model has no barb-ridge mechanics, pulp diffusion or regeneration cycle, and its a, k and dose multipliers are free parameters fitted to the row counts (-5); reverse chimeras are extrapolations (-3)." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-model-fidelity> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> ;
    pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/model-fidelity" ;
    pk:evidenceAgainst "2018-haupaix-avian-plumage-somite-stripes.py L286–L289: Cubic-saturating linearised kinetics, not the rational form in the reference JSON governing_pde <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/469bf3c/2018-haupaix-avian-plumage-somite-stripes.py#L286-L289>",
        "2018-haupaix-avian-plumage-somite-stripes.py L351–L356: Species width from analytic Gaussian threshold with sigma_eff = 1.13 sigma; comment calls it 'PDE-coupled' but no PDE is run <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/469bf3c/2018-haupaix-avian-plumage-somite-stripes.py#L351-L356>" ;
    pk:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-haupaix-avian-plumage-somite-stripes-model-fidelity-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-haupaix-avian-plumage-somite-stripes-model-fidelity-2>,
